===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ja|chichi}}
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|ちち}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|sort=ちち|父|tr=titi}}, from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|sort=ちち|*titi}}.

Still in modern usage.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|ちち|acc=1|dev=1|acc_ref=DJR,NHK|acc2=2|acc2_ref=DJR,NHK|acc2_note={{ja-non-lexical-pitch}}}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|ちち}}

# [[father]]
#: {{ja-x|野比のび助は、主%人%公のび太の'''父'''。|^のび ^のびすけ は、しゅ%じん%こう ^のびた の '''ちち'''。|Nobi Nobisuke is the '''father''' of the protagonist Nobita.}}
#* {{RQ:Wamyō Ruijushō|1|115}}
#*: {{ja-usex|父%　爲%考、和%名%'''知%々'''、日%本%紀%私%記%云%加%曾|ちち%　す%こう、 わ%めい% '''ち%ち'''、 ^に%ほん% ^き% ^し%き% いう% カ%ソ|Father: considered in Japanese as '''''chichi'''''; in the ''{{w|Nihon Shoki Shiki}}'' it is pronounced ''kaso''}}
# {{lb|ja|sort=ちち|by extension|figurative}} a [[father figure]] {{gl|[[male]] [[initiator]] or [[founder]] of something}}
#: {{ja-usex|[[近%代]]%[[医%学]]の'''父'''|きん%だい% い%がく の '''ちち'''|the '''father''' of modern medicine}}
# {{lb|ja|sort=ちち|Christianity}} [[God]], the [[Holy Father]]

=====Usage notes=====
* This term conveys neither positive nor negative connotations. However, using it to describe someone the speaker knows personally is often considered lacking respect, where more polite forms like {{ja-r|お父さん|おとうさん}} are preferred.
* This term is sometimes used in objective narrations, but for this purpose, {{ja-r|父%親|ちち%おや}} is more common.

=====Antonyms=====
* {{antsense|father}} {{ja-r|母|はは|[[mother]]}}

